.TH "PKGEXEC_LINUX_ISOLATED" "3" "" "libpkgexec\-linux" "Version 0.6.2"
.SH NAME
pkgexec_linux_isolated \- private Linux filesystem and network execution contract
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]#include <libpkgexec\-linux/backend.h>\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]isolated_backend::make()\f[R] accepts exact \f[B]interpreter_binding\f[R] values.
\f[B]execute()\f[R] requires a dedicated root\-view directory and exact directory materializations for every declared resource.
.PP
The backend opens roots and resources without following symlinks, clones mount trees, makes the exact root read\-only and \f[CR]nosuid\f[R], applies \f[CR]nosuid,nodev\f[R] plus read\-only or writable attributes to declared resource trees, creates a private mount namespace, attaches resources at their exact logical paths, enters the root, drops capabilities, and executes the exact interpreter descriptor.
.PP
The root tree is read\-only.
Source and package\-input resources must be read\-only.
Workspace, package\-output, private\-temporary, and managed\-target resources must be writable.
Root and resource host paths cannot overlap.
.PP
\f[B]network_policy::allowed\f[R] preserves the caller\[aq]s network namespace.
\f[B]network_policy::denied\f[R] creates a private network namespace whose only link is administratively down loopback.
\f[B]network_policy::loopback_only\f[R] creates the same private view and brings only loopback up.
The backend invokes no network configuration program and inherits no host interface or route into either private view.
.PP
The controlled execution overload composes the same isolated root and network view with request\-bound pidfd cancellation.
Cancellation before the final start gate prevents program execution.
Started cancellation preserves complete stream capture and requires both process\-tree and scratch cleanup verification.
.PP
The supplied root must contain its interpreter and runtime closure.
Persistent device nodes in the exact root are not activated because the root and declared resources are \f[CR]nodev\f[R].
The backend overlays a private execution\-only \f[CR]/dev\f[R] containing deterministic \f[CR]/dev/null\f[R] and imports no ambient host \f[CR]/dev\f[R].
Nested mounts and host pseudo\-filesystems are not inherited.
Exact address\-space, file\-size, and open\-files limits compose with the private filesystem and network views and are sealed before the final start gate.
The backend creates no user or PID namespace and provides no Landlock, cgroup, arbitrary credential, CPU\-time, or execution\-wide process\-count guarantee.
.PP
If filesystem, network, or cancellation realization is unavailable or policy\-restricted, the request is rejected before start.
There is no fallback to a weaker execution policy.
